<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 16 October, from 690 to 1946.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wu-zetian.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">690 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,336 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wu Zetian proclaims herself emperor of China</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a>, long the power behind the Tang throne, took the title of emperor and founded her own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>. She remains the only woman to rule <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in her own name, and expanded recruitment by examination.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-zetian">Wu Zetian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">912 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,114 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Abd al-Rahman III becomes emir of Córdoba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a> became the eighth emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>. He went on to reunite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> and in 929 proclaimed himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, founding the Caliphate of Córdoba; his reign marked the height of Andalusi power.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abd-al-rahman-iii">Abd al-Rahman III</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1384">1384 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">642 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jadwiga is crowned king, not queen, of Poland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Jadwiga, youngest daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-i-of-hungary">Louis I of Hungary</a>, was crowned king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, rather than queen, to highlight her sovereign status. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/union-of-krewo">Union of Krewo</a> she later married the Lithuanian grand duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Jogaila</a>, beginning the dynastic union of Poland and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jadwiga-of-poland">Jadwiga of Poland</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Jourdan's French army wins the Battle of Wattignies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After two days of combat at Wattignies, a French army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-jourdan">Jean-Baptiste Jourdan</a> defeated a Coalition army directed by Prince Josias of Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>. The victory allowed the French to raise the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maubeuge">Maubeuge</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-jourdan">Jean-Baptiste Jourdan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-first-coalition">War of the First Coalition</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1793">1793 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">233 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Antoinette is guillotined in Paris</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a two-day trial before the Revolutionary Tribunal, the former queen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette">Marie Antoinette</a> was executed on the Place de la Révolution. She was 37, and her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xvi">Louis XVI</a> had been executed nine months earlier.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1813">1813 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">213 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Battle of Leipzig begins</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Austrian, Prussian, Russian and Swedish armies attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leipzig">Leipzig</a>. With some 600,000 soldiers engaged over three days, the '<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leipzig">Battle of the Nations</a>' was the largest in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> before the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1916">1916 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">110 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Margaret Sanger opens the first US birth control clinic</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Margaret Sanger, her sister and a colleague opened a birth control clinic in Brownsville, Brooklyn. Police closed it nine days later, but Sanger's campaign led to the organisation that became Planned Parenthood.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ten Nazi leaders are hanged at Nuremberg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ten men sentenced by the International Military Tribunal, including Ribbentrop, Keitel and Streicher, were hanged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a> prison's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gymnasium">gymnasium</a>. Göring had taken poison the night before.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 16 October <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/gian-galeazzo-visconti"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/gian-galeazzo-visconti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Gian Galeazzo Visconti</span><span class="tp">1351–1402</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-ii-of-scotland"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-ii-of-scotland.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James II of Scotland</span><span class="tp">1430–1460</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ito-hirobumi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ito-hirobumi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Itō Hirobumi</span><span class="tp">1841–1909</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/david-ben-gurion"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">David Ben-Gurion</span><span class="tp">1886–1973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/enver-hoxha"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/enver-hoxha.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Enver Hoxha</span><span class="tp">1908–1985</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 16 October <span class="n">12</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/fu-jian-337-385"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/fu-jian-337-385.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Fu Jian (337–385)</span><span class="tp">337–385</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lullus"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lullus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lullus</span><span class="tp">c. 710–786</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/al-hakam-ii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/al-hakam-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">al-Hakam II</span><span class="tp">915–976</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/amadeus-v-count-of-savoy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Amadeus V, Count of Savoy</span><span class="tp">c. 1249–1323</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/luca-signorelli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/luca-signorelli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Luca Signorelli</span><span class="tp">c. 1450–1523</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/antoine-de-lamothe-cadillac"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/antoine-de-lamothe-cadillac.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Antoine de Lamothe Cadillac</span><span class="tp">1658–1730</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/marie-antoinette.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Marie Antoinette</span><span class="tp">1755–1793</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-iii-of-sardinia"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/victor-amadeus-iii-of-sardinia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Victor Amadeus III of Sardinia</span><span class="tp">1726–1796</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/arthur-seyss-inquart"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/arthur-seyss-inquart.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Arthur Seyss-Inquart</span><span class="tp">1892–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-frick"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/wilhelm-frick.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Wilhelm Frick</span><span class="tp">1877–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/liaquat-ali-khan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/liaquat-ali-khan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Liaquat Ali Khan</span><span class="tp">1895–1951</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/martti-ahtisaari"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/martti-ahtisaari.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Martti Ahtisaari</span><span class="tp">1937–2023</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
